Ideas taken from other open-source projects
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Rugol borrows ideas — not code — from the projects below. Where a design is
theirs, it is credited here and in the source file that implements it. Nothing
in this repository is a copy of their source; each item was reimplemented for
Rugol's runtime, which differs in ways that matter (Rugol runs agents
unattended, on a schedule, with no human at the terminal).

If you are one of these authors and think the attribution is wrong or
insufficient, open an issue and it gets fixed.


gstack — https://github.com/garrytan/gstack
  Author: Garry Tan.  License: MIT.
  Consulted at commit state of 2026-08-22.

  1. Hard brakes on destructive commands.
     Their `/careful` skill warns a human before `rm -rf`, a force-push to the
     default branch, or a recursive delete of root, and hard-denies the worst
     of them.
     → Rugol: `core/safety/guards.py`. Reimplemented as `PreToolUse` hooks in
       the runtime rather than as a skill, and every rule is a hard deny with
       no warn tier: gstack has a human to warn, Rugol runs at 8:30 AM with
       nobody watching. The rule set, the anchoring to command position, and
       the deny messages are ours; the idea of shipping brakes at all is
       theirs.

  2. Confining edits to one directory while debugging.
     Their `/freeze` skill stops an agent from making drive-by edits across a
     repo.
     → Rugol: `evaluate_write` in the same module, enforced on Write/Edit
       tool calls instead of by instruction.

  Their broader system — the 23-skill sprint workflow, the GStack Browser,
  GBrain, the telemetry receipts — is deliberately NOT ported. It solves a
  different problem (a human driving a terminal) and duplicates parts Rugol
  already has (the Soul layer, the ontology).


claude-agent-sdk — https://github.com/anthropics/claude-agent-sdk-python
  Author: Anthropic.  License: MIT.  Used as a dependency, not vendored.
  Rugol runs every agent through this SDK and the Claude Code CLI it bundles.


eduagent-gateway (Eduardo Moraga, unpublished)
  The Telegram adapter, the single-instance lock, the attachment download and
  the audio transcription path were ported from this earlier prototype by the
  same author.
